<%!-- How long the newsfeed is: what one arrival carries, what "Load more"
adds, and what a source switch or an opened calendar day asks for — the member
owns the number, the installation sets what an untouched account gets
(/admin/preferences).

The same round numbers the control under the timeline offers, and the same
gesture: press one, it is set — one component draws both
(`PostComponents.page_size_chips/1`), so they cannot drift apart. No Save button
beside them, because a single value with five choices has nothing to collect:
pressing a number IS the save, and a two-step form here would be the one place
in the app where this control behaves differently from its twin on /feed. --%>
<.settings_shell user={@user} active={:feed_page_size} title={gettext("Posts in your feed")}>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{Vutuv.Prefs.label(:feed_page_size)}</.section_title>
      <p id="feed-page-size-hint" class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {Vutuv.Prefs.hint(:feed_page_size)}
      </p>

      <.form
        :let={f}
        for={@changeset}
        action={~p"/settings/feed_page_size"}
        id="feed-page-size-form"
        class="mt-5"
      >
        <.form_error changeset={@changeset} />

        <.page_size_chips
          id="settings-page-size"
          current={Vutuv.Prefs.feed_page_size(@user)}
          label={Vutuv.Prefs.label(:feed_page_size)}
          mode={:submit}
        />

        {error_tag(f, :feed_page_size)}
      </.form>

      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "You can change this under the feed itself as well, right below the “Load more” button."
        )}
      </p>
    </.card>

    <%!-- Back to inheriting the installation default — the shape the bandwidth
    page's reset uses, outside the card and only once the member holds a value
    of their own. --%>
    <div :if={Vutuv.Prefs.customized_in_group?(@user, :feed_size)} class="-mt-3">
      <.link
        href={~p"/settings/feed_page_size/reset"}
        method="post"
        id="reset-feed-page-size"
        class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-400 dark:hover:text-slate-200"
      >
        {gettext("Reset to the site defaults")}
      </.link>
    </div>
  </div>
</.settings_shell>
